session:pr797Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #749 was a deferred nice-to-have noted in epic #182's description (caught during an epic-completeness audit, never filed on its own): now that owl_functional_parser (#182) and manchester_parser (#178) both target the same owl_ontology::Ontology type with working parsers and serializers, a cross-syntax round-trip test (parse as one syntax, serialize as the other, re-parse, compare axiom sets) was possible but had never been written -- only same-syntax round-trips existed (owl_functional_parser/tests/serialize_roundtrip.rs, manchester_parser/tests/serialize_roundtrip.rs)." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:797 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr797Decision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr797 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr797Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Added tests/cross_syntax_roundtrip.rs (top-level, matching the existing cross-crate tests/manchester_roundtrip.rs convention) with two tests, one per direction, each round-tripping a representative multi-construct fixture (classes, SubClassOf/EquivalentClasses/DisjointClasses, object/data property domain/range/characteristics/sub-property/inverse, a nested intersection+existential-restriction class expression, and ABox same/different-individual assertions) and comparing the resulting axiom HashSet both against the original and against an independently hand-written fixture in the target syntax -- the same bar the existing same-syntax round-trip tests use. Test-only change, no production code touched. Sanity-checked the tests are genuinely meaningful (not tautological) by temporarily breaking owl_functional_parser::serialize to drop all SubClassOf axioms and confirming the test failed with exactly that diff, then reverting." ;
    agp:alternative "Deliberately excluded anonymous individuals from the fixture: the two serializers group/order axioms differently, which could legitimately assign different anon-individual ids across syntaxes even when the axiom sets are semantically identical, making a naive id-sensitive comparison flaky for reasons unrelated to a real round-trip bug. Out of scope for this issue's 'representative fixture' ask; left as a known gap rather than building anon-individual-aware comparison logic here." .
